    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **14 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the registration-date feature for `POST /api/owners`: when no `registrationDate` is supplied it defaults to the server's current date, and `registrationDate` is returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`, optional) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Because `Owner` is `allOf` `OwnerFields`, this makes the field both accepted on the request and returned on the response. The `format: date` generates a `LocalDate` on the DTOs, which Jackson serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java` (entity)** \u2014 Added a `registrationDate` `LocalDate` field mapped to a `registration_date` column, plus getter/setter. MapStruct maps it by name in both directions automatically.\n\n3. **`BuildOwner.java`** \u2014 After mapping the request to the entity, defaults `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when it wasn't supplied; a supplied value is preserved.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres` `schema.sql`) \u2014 Added the `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table.\n\n5. **Seed data** (`hsqldb`, `mysql` `data.sql`) \u2014 These use positional `INSERT INTO owners VALUES(...)`, so I added a trailing `NULL` for the new column (h2/postgres use explicit column lists and needed no change).\n\nBoth new tests (`coreDefaultsToToday`, `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate`) pass, and no existing tests regressed.",
